  "question": {
    "text": "Two polaroids <math> <mi>A</mi> </math> and <math> <mi>B</mi> </math> are placed with their polaroid axes <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> to each other as shown in the figure. A plane polarised light passes through the polaroid <math> <mi>A</mi> </math> and after passing through it, intensity of light becomes <math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>. What is the intensity of finally transmitted light, after passing through the polaroid <math> <mi>B</mi> </math>?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/Live.PNG\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 172px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
